answer:
@Ahmet. The DFT equation you posted does not compute an array of complex numbers. For any single given integer value of frequency-domain index $k$ the equation tells us how to compute the single complex-valued number $X[k]$ based on $N$ samples of $x[n]$.
Also, please do not fall into the trap of thinking when the DFT is used as a filter that some sort of downward frequency translation occurs. It does not. When used in real-time as a filter, each real-time bin output of the DFT is the output of a bandpass filter. I explain this idea at:
https://www.dsprelated.com/showarticle/187.php

